title: 'Cid Debrief: Portable MCP-config PATH fix (7.8.2 addition), run architect+claude-code-guide→b'
summary: 'Portable MCP-config PATH fix (7.8.2 addition), run architect+claude-code-guide→builder→tester, then founder-narrowed in review. Root cause: generated .mcp.json launches paradigm-mcp with a bare command that fails to resolve when Claude Code spawns it in a PATH-deficient (macOS GUI/non-login) context lacking /opt/homebrew/bin. Fix: new mcpServerEnv() helper emits an env.PATH APPEND form (${PATH}:/opt/homebrew/bin:...) that augments (never replaces) the inherited PATH. SCOPED TO CLAUDE CODE ONLY after review caught that the as-built version applied risky env to 4 clients whose ${VAR} expansion is unconfirmed (literal ${PATH} would destroy PATH; static list would regress nvm/Volta users). All other clients keep the bare command (no regression) pending expansion verification (follow-up T-2026-09-01-005). 93 adapter tests pass. Not yet committed at debrief time.'
